invariant: INV-17
file: src/mldsa_vector.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mldsa-vector
reason: mld_vector_pointwise_acc ends with VZEROUPPER where it had
  VZEROALL. VZEROUPPER clears bits 128 to 255 alone, so the low halves
  of the vector registers still hold the last group's products when the
  call returns. In the signer those are products with s1, s2 or t0.
  Every coefficient stays right. bin/mldsa_vector_equiv_test sets every
  bit of ymm0 to ymm15, calls each entry and stores the sixteen
  registers in one block of assembly, and requires every stored word
  zero. Only an x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds the
  binary for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64.

--- old
        store(acc->coeffs + i, _mm256_add_epi32(sum, montgomery_multiply(x, y)));
    }
    _mm256_zeroall();
--- new
        store(acc->coeffs + i, _mm256_add_epi32(sum, montgomery_multiply(x, y)));
    }
    _mm256_zeroupper();
